From: Kernel security backport review <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ip6mr: drop dst before reports and unresolved queues

Adapt both ownership changes to the local queue-limit/dev control flow.
Report copies and unresolved packets no longer retain receive-side dst
references beyond the RCU lifetime. Forwarding resolves its own output dst.

CVE: CVE-2026-90111
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/235b42b5860189eb8c27c36435ad932cae65a734]

diff --git a/net/ipv6/ip6mr.c b/net/ipv6/ip6mr.c
--- a/net/ipv6/ip6mr.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/ip6mr.c
@@ -1136,10 +1136,10 @@
 	msg->im6_src = ipv6_hdr(pkt)->saddr;
 	msg->im6_dst = ipv6_hdr(pkt)->daddr;
 
-	skb_dst_set(skb, dst_clone(skb_dst(pkt)));
 	skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY;
 	}
 
+	skb_dst_drop(skb);
 	mrt6msg_netlink_event(mrt, skb);
 
 	/* Deliver to user space multicast routing algorithms */
@@ -1219,6 +1219,7 @@
 			skb->dev = dev;
 			skb->skb_iif = dev->ifindex;
 		}
+		skb_dst_drop(skb);
 		skb_queue_tail(&c->_c.mfc_un.unres.unresolved, skb);
 		err = 0;
 	}
